{% regular %}Our {% /regular %}{% regular %}[Sacred Heart Primary School, Fitzroy](/?projects=sacred-heart-primary-school-fitzroy-junior-school-renovations){% /regular %}{% regular %} was recognised with commendations in two categories at the 2022 Victoria and Tasmania Chapter Learning Environment Australia (LEA) Awards:{% /regular %}

- {% regular %}[Category 6: Modernisation – Small](https://learningenvironments.awardsplatform.com/gallery/QdGPOGrY/jKWwwoND?search=7b7025766b97a307-30){% /regular %}

- {% regular %}[Category 7: Small Projects Value Under AU$2 Million](https://learningenvironments.awardsplatform.com/gallery/QdGPOGrY/aWWYoEEM?search=7b7025766b97a307-33){% /regular %}

{% wideImage src="/src/assets/media/sacred-heart-primary-school-fitzroy-recognised/2022/11/69A9574-1-10.jpg" alt="Sacred Heart Primary School, lockers on the lobby" /%}

{% regular %}Excerpts from the judges citations for each commendation include:{% /regular %}

> {% regular %}“This is a small project with a big impact. The objective was to transform learning areas and adjacent outdoor play areas to enable the delivery of contemporary pedagogy in order to improve learning outcomes.”{% /regular %}

{% regular %}“With the relatively limited budget, the project team was able to maximise use of what was previously unused areas of the building to create vibrant, inviting and more flexible learning spaces that is able to accommodate more agile ways of teaching and learning creating a built environment that is more aligned to the school’s pedagogy.”{% /regular %}
